.TH DAQ-NETWORK-VERIFY.SH 1 "2026-09-10" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
daq-network-verify.sh \- sweep the DAQ private networks and report live hosts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B daq-network-verify.sh
[\fB\-N\fR \fInetworks\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIdir\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B daq-network-verify.sh
is a diagnostic for the DAQ private networks. It pings every address on
each configured network with \fBnmap \-sn\fR so that the responding
hosts appear in the local ARP table, dumps the ARP and routing tables,
and then reports which hosts answered on each network.
.PP
Three networks are swept by default:
.PP
.RS
.nf
control  192.168.6.0/24
data     192.168.7.0/24
ipmi     192.168.157.0/24
.fi
.RE
.PP
Networks are given as \fIlabel\fB=\fIcidr\fR so the report can name
them; a bare CIDR is accepted and labelled \fInetwork\fR.
.PP
The routing table is read with whichever tool is present: \fBip route
show\fR, then \fBroute \-n\fR, then \fBnetstat \-rn\fR, so the script
works on both Linux and macOS.
.SH OPTIONS
Configuration precedence is command line, then environment variable,
then .env file, then built-in default.
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-\-networks " " \fILIST\fR
Space- or comma-separated networks to sweep, each optionally
\fIlabel\fB=\fIcidr\fR. Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_NETWORKS\fR.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIDIR\fR
Directory for the dumps. Environment:
\fBMU2EDAQ_NETVERIFY_DIR\fR. Default: the current directory.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-skip\-scan
Do not run \fBnmap\fR; report from the ARP table as it already stands.
This makes the command safe to run when a scan is unwelcome, and
removes the \fBnmap\fR dependency.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print what would be done and write nothing. Requires no tools at all.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Trace execution with \fBset \-x\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DAQ_NETWORK_VERIFY_SH_OPTS
Extra options, prepended to the command line.
.SH FILES
Written into the output directory:
.TP
.I arp_table.txt
The full sorted ARP table.
.TP
.I routing_table.txt
The routing table.
.TP
.I filtered_arp_table.txt
Only the ARP entries belonging to the swept networks.
.SH NOTES
Sweeping a /24 takes a few seconds per network. \fBnmap\fR is required
unless \fB\-\-skip\-scan\fR or \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR is given.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 when the sweep and report completed, 1 when \fBnmap\fR is
needed but missing or no networks were given, and 2 for an
unrecognised option.
.SH EXAMPLES
Sweep the standard networks into \fI/tmp\fR:
.PP
.RS
.nf
daq-network-verify.sh -o /tmp
.fi
.RE
.PP
Report from the existing ARP table without scanning:
.PP
.RS
.nf
daq-network-verify.sh --skip-scan
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check one extra network:
.PP
.RS
.nf
daq-network-verify.sh -N "mgmt=10.1.0.0/24"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR daq-cluster-cp (1),
.BR daq-status.sh (1),
.BR nmap (1),
.BR arp (8)
